Silo patch 0007 — winecoreaudio: upstream's device-period sizing and SpatialMixer down-mix

Origin: upstream Wine (gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine), nine commits to dlls/winecoreaudio.drv/coreaudio.c,
squashed and applied in order. They apply cleanly to crossover-sources-26.3.0, whose coreaudio.c is Wine 11.0's
plus 18 lines. License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like Wine.
  56a4347a  Giovanni Mascellani  winecoreaudio.drv: Avoid a division by zero.
  07c7fcc8  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio: Set the requested period frame size when creating audio streams.
  8e09602c  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio: Add a helper to get device sample rate.
  da0b0847  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio: Return the actual Core Audio device period frame size.
  199ae1d3  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio.drv: Move some helpers.
  d20f6c71  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio.drv: Add a get_format_channel_mask() helper.
  3e29c363  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio.drv: Add a ca_get_layout_channel_mask() helper.
  8cf64080  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio.drv: Add a get_device_channel_mask() helper.
  0c61795b  Zhiyi Zhang  winecoreaudio.drv: Add a SpatialMixer audio unit to mix input audio when necessary.
(da0b0847 also touches dlls/mmdevapi/tests/render.c; that test hunk is left out.) Highball carries the same two
fixes as its own patches 0015 and 0023.

Why Silo carries it: UNCHARTED: Legacy of Thieves Collection crackles on a stereo Mac in its default output mode
("Automatico (Tradizionale)"), which renders an 8-channel 7.1 stream through a plain IAudioClient. Measured
2026-10-31 with thread-safe counters in this driver: the data reaching Wine is clean (0 underruns, 0 samples beyond
full scale, peak 0.11 over 97-126 s), so the artefact appeared when the 8 channels were folded to the device's 2.
With this patch the stream is mixed by AUSpatialMixer and the device buffer matches Wine's period. The user
verified it the same day: no crackle in the Traditional mode, on the speakers and on AirPods. (The game's
"Spaziale" mode was already clean.)

